{
    "background_story": "Alexandra was a brilliant and meticulous architect, known for her attention to detail and passion for historical preservation. Her latest project was the restoration of a 19th-century mansion, where she became fascinated with the intricate architrave that adorned the entrance. As she carefully disassembled and restored the ornate carvings, she discovered a hidden compartment containing a letter from the original architect. The letter revealed the story behind the mansion's design and the significance of the architrave, which was meant to symbolize the connection between heaven and earth. Inspired by her discovery, Alexandra designed a modern extension to the mansion, incorporating a stunning architrave that paid homage to the original while showcasing her own unique style. Her work was met with critical acclaim, and she was hailed as a master of her craft.",
